  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/47b77320474a559f69e6ef08b8f6638aac920b05014820ab1b4b82690059c997.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nThe equation of the trend line is $y=-0.5x+9.$ Assuming this trend continues, estimate the value of $x$ when $y=2.$",
  "worked_solution": "We can estimate the required value by substituting $y=2$ into the equation of the trend line and solving for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+9 \\\\ 2 & =-0.5x+9 \\\\ 2+0.5x & =9 \\\\ 0.5x & =7 \\\\ x & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $y=2$ we have $x\u224814.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=2$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
